   <ClinicalAssociation>
    <association_text>Enterococcaceae bloomed significantly in the gut microbiota of critically ill ICU patients compared to healthy controls, representing one of two dominant pathobiont families (alongside Enterobacteriaceae) expanding during critical illness-associated gut dysbiosis.</association_text>
    <content_hash>ef2e4e92c14490d56497a5aa34ec34ec54c81d69b87a0bdbe083c2608f84f0ed</content_hash>
    <evidence_grade>E2</evidence_grade>
